<header><p class="st-kicker">colony · Central and Southern Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Diego-Suarez Colony</h1><p class="st-meta">1885 CE – 1896 CE · capital Diego-Suarez</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A small French colony around the great natural harbour of northern Madagascar, gained in 1885 and kept as a naval base.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The treaty ending the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/franco-hova-war">Franco-Hova War</a> in 1885 gave <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> the bay of Diego-Suarez, now <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antsiranana">Antsiranana</a>, at the northern tip of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madagascar">Madagascar</a>, one of the finest natural harbours in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-ocean">Indian Ocean</a>. France organised it as a separate colony.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The colony was essentially a naval base and coaling station with a garrison town around it, with salt works and a meat-canning plant. It attracted Comoran, Indian, Arab and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/criollo-people">Creole</a> migrants alongside Malagasy workers, and its harbour was fortified as a key point of French naval power in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-ocean">Indian Ocean</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> annexed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madagascar">Madagascar</a>, Diego-Suarez was merged into the colony of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/french-madagascar">French Madagascar</a> in 1896. It remained a major naval base, captured by British forces in 1942 during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-madagascar">Battle of Madagascar</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="colony, 1885 CE – 1896 CE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 64 H80 L70 78 H30 Z"/><path d="M50 64 V18"/><path d="M50 22 L72 56 H50"/><path d="M50 28 L32 56 H50"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">colony</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Central and Southern Africa</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:97.21%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1885 CE – 1896 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>colony</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Diego-Suarez</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Islam, Christianity, Malagasy traditional religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Malagasy, French</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/madagascar">Madagascar</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Diego-Suarez, Antsiranana</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1890&amp;focus=diego-suarez-colony" aria-label="Diego-Suarez Colony on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5934 2866 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Diego-Suarez Colony lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5054 728h0M6286 3134h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6254 3122h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M6254 3122h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Madagascar. <a href="/atlas?year=1890&amp;focus=diego-suarez-colony">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
